# Trivy suppression list.
#
# RULES FOR THIS FILE
#   1. Every entry needs a CVE id, an expiry date, and a written justification.
#   2. "It is noisy" is not a justification. "Not reachable because X" is.
#   3. An expired entry stops suppressing and the pipeline fails again on purpose -
#      that is the mechanism that stops suppressions becoming permanent.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# The file is currently empty, and that is the intended state. Both package trees
# were brought to `npm audit` clean while this pipeline was built (unused multer
# dropped, nodemailer moved to 9.x, axios and react-router patched), so there is
# nothing to suppress. Add an entry only when a finding is genuinely unfixable and
# genuinely not exploitable in this application, and say why here.
